RG DS Play: a ScummVM game goes on from where it was left.

The core has no save states, and ScummVM autosaves only every five minutes: a
short session left nothing. The first request to leave (a quit, or a return to the launcher) now writes the autosave (not
where the game cannot save, nor over a save of the player's own in that slot),
SCUMM writes it as its loop ends (it saves from the loop), and a game whose
autosave is there loads it as it starts.

